dogecoin.text:
@alex Well, if you want a store of value, Bitcoin is your answer. 

Dogecoin and Ethereum have no limit (like fiat currencies), and Ethereum had a "bailout" in 2016.

Also, no fiat currency in human history has lasted more than a few hundred years.

@WholeMarsBlog (IANAFA (I am not a financial adviser)) Lol Bitcoin is the  asset people should be quickly figuring out how to use and store. 

Bitcoin incurs no costs for doing nothing. It's the ultimate store of value.

If he marketed dogecoin or an altcoin (shitcoin), that would be scammy.

@WholeMarsBlog It's not impossible, it just misses the point entirely.

The idea behind crypto is supposed to be more freedom. Adopting Dogecoin as a standard currency means more centralization which results in less freedom.

Why would you want that?

@WholeMarsBlog That depends on your reality. 

Regular people are not "investing in Dogecoin" because things are going well.

Twitter should let you add a "/s" for sarcasm.

@JamesSurowiecki Some Dogecoin wallets have over 1billion USD in doge.

People are treating Dogecoin as an actual investment because of a lack of confidence in the dollar. 

A joke cryptocurrency seems more sound than holding dollars.

